From: Muhammed Dali <dali.nira.12.1453kerinyoli@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] [GTK] AcceleratedSurface: destroy the release-buffers timer
 synchronously on its run loop

AcceleratedSurface::willDestroyCompositingRunLoop() dispatched the reset of
m_releaseUnusedBuffersTimer to the compositing run loop. The ThreadedCompositor
stops that run loop right afterwards, and a task still pending when its thread
exits is dropped unrun. The lambda's protectedThis can then be the surface's
last reference, so the surface, and with it the still-active RunLoop timer, is
destroyed on the main run loop, and ~TimerBase() aborts the web process
(WebKitGTK 2.54.1, about 2% of window lifetimes in DaliNira's multi-tab flow).

Reset the timer synchronously on the compositing run loop instead.

Changed by DaliNira on 2026-10-08 for its private WebKitGTK 2.54.1 runtime.
Validated: 0 crashes in 500 window lifetimes (unpatched control: 3 in 40).
Not yet merged upstream. The file is under the BSD-2-Clause terms in its
header; this change is offered under the same terms.

--- a/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/AcceleratedSurface.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/CoordinatedGraphics/AcceleratedSurface.cpp
@@ -44,6 +44,7 @@
 #include <wtf/SafeStrerror.h>
 #include <wtf/SystemTracing.h>
 #include <wtf/TZoneMallocInlines.h>
+#include <wtf/threads/BinarySemaphore.h>
 
 WTF_IGNORE_WARNINGS_IN_THIRD_PARTY_CODE_BEGIN
 #include <skia/core/SkCanvas.h>
@@ -1033,11 +1034,21 @@
 #endif
 
     // m_releaseUnusedBuffersTimer is owned by the compositing run loop and its destructor stops it, so
-    // destroy it on that run loop's thread rather than here on the main thread.
+    // destroy it on that run loop's thread rather than here on the main thread. Do it synchronously:
+    // the compositing run loop is stopped right after this (its WorkQueue goes away with the
+    // ThreadedCompositor), and a task dispatched to it may then never run; it is dropped when the
+    // thread exits, the surface is destroyed on the main run loop and the still-active timer with it.
     if (RefPtr compositingRunLoop = std::exchange(m_compositingRunLoop, nullptr)) {
-        compositingRunLoop->dispatch([protectedThis = Ref { *this }] {
-            protectedThis->m_releaseUnusedBuffersTimer = nullptr;
-        });
+        if (compositingRunLoop->isCurrent())
+            m_releaseUnusedBuffersTimer = nullptr;
+        else {
+            BinarySemaphore semaphore;
+            compositingRunLoop->dispatch([this, &semaphore] {
+                m_releaseUnusedBuffersTimer = nullptr;
+                semaphore.signal();
+            });
+            semaphore.wait();
+        }
     }
 #if PLATFORM(GTK) || ENABLE(WPE_PLATFORM)
     WebProcess::singleton().parentProcessConnection()->removeMessageReceiver(Messages::AcceleratedSurface::messageReceiverName(), m_id);
